From c80200014227968194610d6710c344aaa463f372 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:10:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the sparse direct solvers of oneMKL

MKLPardisoSolver (sequential, PARDISO) and MKLClusterSparseSolver
(parallel, the Cluster Sparse Solver, the rows being distributed as the
ones of the matrix of hypre) call oneMKL directly, when MFEM is built
with MFEM_USE_MKL_PARDISO or MFEM_USE_MKL_CPARDISO, not through
mfem::PardisoSolver and mfem::CPardisoSolver, which check the errors of
oneMKL with MFEM_ASSERT only, read and write the vectors on the host
without synchronizing them, and give the whole matrix to the symmetric
types of PARDISO.

The matrix is copied on the host in the compressed row format of oneMKL
(sorted columns, upper triangle for the symmetric types, options
Symmetric and PositiveDefinite), the vectors are copied on the host. The
analysis is reused for the operators of the same pattern (option
ReuseAnalysis, number of analyses given by getNumberOfAnalyses). A failed
analysis or factorization throws a CollectiveFailure on all the
processes. oneMKL perturbs the small pivots and factorizes a singular
matrix without error: as for cuDSS, a resolution is reported as converged
only if its residual is lower than 1e-3 times the right hand side.
